  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "Stability table, (3,1) block at R=40/nr=40: the original lists 5.4e-5 (x3), 1.9e-4 (x3), 3.7e-4 as 'zero modes, then continuum'. 1.939e-4 (x3) is the first continuum level (mine 1.937e-4); 3.73e-4 (x3) is the unresolved iso-rotation zero-mode triplet, which lies above it. So zero modes are not the lowest eigenvalues at that mesh.",
   "suggested_fix": "Relabel the R=40 column; quote converged zero-mode values from a higher-order basis (cubic B-splines: 7.5e-8 and 4.1e-6 at R=40, 1.9e-6 and 3.7e-5 at R=20)."
  },
