   "suggested_fix": "Say 'the element exp(2 pi T3^L) (image of -1 in SU(2)_L)'."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "The argument that no velocity-linear term can shift the singlet constraint ('must be a character of the stabiliser's Lie algebra') is incomplete as stated: an SU(2)_short-invariant linear term along the (3,1) directions is not excluded by that argument, only by spatial-rotation (right SU(2)_L) invariance. The conclusion is unchanged. Also, AMENDED is applied to a PLAN section 3 literature note, not to a seed claim.",
   "suggested_fix": "Add 'and right SU(2)_L (rotation) invariance' to the argument; call the PLAN 3.5 item 'refined', not AMENDED."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "Citation precision: Mayanskiy 1611.04070 Table 2 lists only the non-regular A1^4 and A1^28; indices 1 (A1) and 3 (A1~) are given in the list right after Table 2 (Table 1 has the regular subalgebras). Prop. 4.1 matches as cited.",
   "suggested_fix": "Cite 'Mayanskiy section 4 (Table 2 and the list following it)'."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "description": "'E2 parameters' were taken as the rounded PLAN ANW point (129 MeV, 5.45). E2's own fit is F_pi = 129.26 MeV, e = 5.444, giving M = 865.75, 1/I1 = 195.33, 1/I2 = 512.69 MeV, so the 14-1 gap is 708.0 instead of 708.9 MeV. Declared deviation; effect <= 0.3%.",
   "suggested_fix": "Optionally add the ladder at E2's fitted point, or say 'PLAN's rounded ANW point' wherever 'E2 parameters' appears."
